      scope = "Accepted text: “Nickel-authored fault schedules MUST use closed descriptor alternatives and MUST validate finite ordering, action-specific fields, VM/link target ranges, partition-set shape, and profile bounds without claiming application or observation.”\nImplementation: `contracts/evidence/fault-schedule-profile.ncl:1-111`, closed `Descriptor` alternatives, strict time ordering, target bounds, disjoint/nonempty/unique partition sets, action ranges, finite maximum and exact intent-only scope. `profile/schedule.rs:29-220`, `FaultDescriptor::validate` and `FaultScheduleProfile::validate`, independently revalidate and convert into runtime faults.\nTests: `evidence_contracts.rs:405-409`, `run_nickel_examples`, rejects target/order/partition/identity/action fixtures; inspected overlapping partition fixture supplies `[0,1]` and `[1,2]`. `profile/tests.rs:198`, `finite_schedule_rejects_unknown_fields_target_and_order_substitution`.\nLimit: only the declared finite descriptor alternatives are supported. These are configuration rejection outcomes, not runtime fault attempts/effects.",
