      scope = "Accepted text: “Profile generation MUST be an explicit shell workflow that binds source, imports, contract, evaluator/profile, and deterministic JSON projection identities with BLAKE3, while runtime Rust MUST revalidate external JSON and MUST NOT invoke Nickel in simulator, campaign, or replay hot paths.”\nImplementation: `profile_projection.rs:44-105`, `check_profile_projections`/`build_receipt`, explicitly evaluate and bind source/contract/import/evaluator/projection; `:141-165`, exact evaluator version; `profile_projection_verification.rs:12-101`, trusted-spec/path/header/source/import/canonical-projection verification without evaluator execution; `profile_projection_spec.rs`, trusted specs. Runtime DTO validators above retain external-input checks. `docs/simulator-campaign-profile-boundary.md`, “Projection workflow”, documents the explicit shell boundary.\nTests: `profile_projection_tests.rs:46`, `verifier_accepts_only_the_trusted_fixture`; `:52`, `verifier_rejects_projection_substitution`; `:63`, `verifier_rejects_joint_projection_and_receipt_substitution`; `:74`, source+receipt substitution; `:85`, bound artifact path substitution; `:101`, missing/extra/duplicate/reordered imports; `:116`, header/non-claim substitution; `:136`, unknown/missing fields.\nLimit: evaluator identity is the reviewed version string bound by BLAKE3, not a measured executable-binary digest. No hot-path invocation was found in the inspected runtime profile conversion implementations.",
