      scope = "Accepted text: “Passing Nickel profile validation MUST establish only reviewed pre-run shape and declared invariants; Rust MUST retain construction, external-input validation, execution, fault applicability/application/observation, checkpointing, replay, progress, reports, and receipt authority.”\nMapping: exact intent-only scope strings in all four contracts; `profile_projection.rs:10-15`, `NON_CLAIMS`; `profile_projection_verification.rs:68-85`, exact header/non-claim validation; Rust conversions above construct the runtime DTOs only after validation. `docs/simulator-campaign-profile-boundary.md`, “Ownership”, “Campaign and resume boundary”, “Non-claims”, explicitly reserve the listed authorities.\nAdversarial tests: `profile_projection_tests.rs:116`, `verifier_rejects_header_and_non_claim_substitution`; `profile/tests.rs:42,68,198` reject injected runtime `elapsed` fields; simulator scope negative fixture is executed by `run_nickel_examples`.\nLimit: supports the ownership/claim boundary, not successful execution of those runtime systems.",
