      implementation = [],
      tests = [],
      reason = "Accepted text: “GIVEN ChaosControl builds profile and evidence checks / WHEN cohort admission runs / THEN every Nickel command MUST use the exact reviewed evaluator”.\nPartial implementation: `flake.nix:6,69-77,112-149`, `exactNickel`, package overlay and `nickelCohortCheck`, bind revision `1320a983e6c3d1e2fb53dd2464b084b4903b1426` and exact version output. `profile_projection.rs:141-165`, `validate_evaluator`, checks the version before generation.\nUnmet subclaim: not every direct Rust Nickel command checks that evaluator. `crates/chaoscontrol-evidence/src/evidence_contracts.rs:452-455`, `nickel_command`, and `src/bin/check-contract-registry.rs:74-82`, `nickel_export_command`, select any executable named `nickel` from PATH. The registry command launches it without an exact-version admission. Nix constrains PATH inside its own rail, not every direct invocation.\nTest limitation: `profile_projection_tests.rs:35`, `evaluator_planning_requires_the_exact_path_command_without_fallback`, checks only command planning/absence, not identity of a PATH executable.",
      accepted_source = ".cairn/specs/nickel-toolchain/spec.md",
