      implementation = [],
      tests = [],
      reason = "Accepted text: “The rail MUST include positive and negative profile, input-admission, boot, module, BPF, bound, cleanup, receipt, wiring, KVM, and evidence-role fixtures and MUST preserve current receipts for at least one selected boot, module, and BPF case before archive.”\nInspected substantial pure tests in `kernel_bundle_validation.rs:1027-1444` include scoped receipt, role-confused input, cleanup/nonclaim gaps, transcript rejection, blocked KVM, missing observations, exact image requirements, broader roles, unsupported boot facts/bounds, scenario-specific negatives, synthetic module/BPF failures, exit-bound and stale image cases. Retained historical `.cairn/archive/2026-07-16-add-kernel-bundle-validation-rail/evidence/mantle-private-kfunc-exact-kvm-receipt-2026-07-15.json` records one passed old positive private-kfunc run, with only uname/module-loader/attach-detach cleanup markers.\nUnmet: no Nickel profile/admission/wiring fixture suite for missing capabilities above, no real triggered BPF typed-event evidence, no real module taint/signature observations, and the July receipt is not a current production-readiness execution receipt. Synthetic error DTOs do not prove guest negative behavior. No current focused/KVM/dependency/docs/Cairn gate execution was performed or claimed by this audit.\n\n# High-value distinctions for the parent\n\n1. The clearest direct requirement contradiction is `chaoscontrol.vm_cohort.source`: accepted `ab123e...`, actual Cargo/Nix/locks/check `0953ab...`.\n2. The strongest profile-source mappings are run/simulator/campaign/schedule shape admission and trusted projection substitution rejection. Ownership-registry enforcement and exhaustive fixture coverage remain real gaps.\n3. eBPF raw payloads are coerced/truncated; cleanup success is asserted after Drop; actual producer-affinity admission is absent. These are implementation gaps, not missing marker syntax.\n4. Kernel smoke is not the accepted full kernel-bundle validation system. In particular there is no Nickel contract, canonical upstream receipt admission, identity-bound guest readiness, module taint/signature observation or BPF trigger/event oracle.\n5. The SDK reference/guidance/local-schema and WalTier source/oracle/boundary are genuine documentation requirements that can be mapped to actual current text without runtime-proof inflation. SDK full-surface mapping and WalTier adversarial documentation verification are not complete.\n6. Do not promote historical archive prose or retained July smoke artifacts into a current test pass. Do not modify historical production-readiness receipts to close these gaps.",
